      "id": "techcon-gh-infrastructure",
      "title": "Techcon GH LLC – Infrastructure Deployment",
      "domain": "Systems Engineering",
      "difficulty": "Advanced",
      "sections": [
        {
          "id": "instructions",
          "title": "Instructions",
          "summary": "This project defines the technical requirements for deploying a centralized Windows Server infrastructure for Techcon GH LLC.",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "paragraphs": [
                "Each section represents a domain of responsibility within the environment.",
                "The requirements specify what must be implemented. The method of implementation is not provided.",
                "The environment must be built on a local lab system using virtualization or equivalent infrastructure.",
                "All configuration must align with the specifications defined in each section."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "scenario",
          "title": "Scenario",
          "summary": "Business and deployment context for the Techcon GH LLC environment.",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "paragraphs": [
                "Techcon GH LLC is a technology consulting firm standardizing the infrastructure for its New York office. The current environment lacks centralized identity management, structured data access, and consistent system configuration.",
                "The organization requires a domain-based environment that supports controlled access to resources, organized administration, centralized storage, and policy-based configuration.",
                "The infrastructure must support the following departments: Sales, Marketing, Operations, Human Resources, and IT.",
                "The IT department includes the following operational teams: Network Operations Center (NOC), Security Operations Center (SOC), and Datacenter Operations.",
                "The completed environment must provide centralized authentication, structured directory services, secure file access, and consistent endpoint configuration."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
